# Security Rules (NEVER BYPASS)

## Secrets & Environment Variables
- NEVER hardcode secrets, API keys, passwords, or tokens
- NEVER commit `.env` files or credentials
- NEVER log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, PII)
- Always use environment variables via `process.env` or `import.meta.env`

## Authentication
- NEVER bypass authentication middleware
- NEVER expose internal user IDs in URLs (use slugs or UUIDs)
- Always validate JWT tokens server-side
- Always hash passwords with bcrypt (cost factor 10+)

## API Security
- Always validate and sanitize user input with Zod
- Always use parameterized queries (Mongoose handles this)
- Never trust client-side data for authorization decisions
- Always check user permissions in controllers

## File Uploads
- Validate file types server-side (not just extension)
- Limit file sizes (5MB max for images)
- Store in R2/S3, never in git or local filesystem

## What to NEVER Generate
```typescript
// ❌ NEVER
const apiKey = "sk-1234567890"
console.log("User password:", password)
localStorage.setItem("password", pwd)

// ✅ ALWAYS
const apiKey = process.env.API_KEY
// Never log passwords
localStorage.setItem("token", jwt) // Only tokens, never passwords
```
